.TH scan_8longn 3
.SH NAME
scan_8longn \- parse an unsigned long integer in octal from a string
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/scan.h>

size_t \fBscan_8longn\fR(const char *\fIsrc\fR, size_t \fIn\fR, unsigned long *\fIdest\fR);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan_8longn\fR parses an unsigned long integer in octal (base 8) notation
from the string \fIsrc\fR, limited to at most \fIn\fR characters.
The result is stored in \fIdest\fR.

It stops reading when it encounters a non-octal digit, when \fIn\fR
characters have been consumed, or when it detects that the value would overflow
an \fBunsigned long\fR.

.SH RETURN VALUE
\fBscan_8longn\fR returns the number of bytes actually read from \fIsrc\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
scan_ulong(3), scan_8long(3)